  "narrative": "H38 strongly extends the accepted feature_065/outcome_013 result to the lower half of feature_043: the signed estimate is +0.116 with the entire 95% interval above the approximate outcome_013 clinical threshold (~0.027). Because the estimates are already signed to direction -1, the raw association is a more negative outcome_013 dependency score for feature_065=1. I accept it as a dataset-internal association. H39 provides no support for stronger effect modification across the feature_043 median split: the interaction estimate is essentially null and the point is opposite the hypothesized direction, while the upper half and lower half main effects in H28 and H38 are nearly identical. I reject the specific stronger-high-feature_043 interaction claim, while noting the interval is wide enough that a moderate interaction is not precisely excluded. The cross-outcome feature_065 panel under high feature_043 is mostly weak: H40, H41, H42, H24, H26, H30, H31, and H32 have point estimates that are small, opposite, or interval-inclusive, and many are near threshold; I leave them unresolved and deferred rather than accept them because this was a multi-outcome screen and the small feature_043-high cells make unstable estimates plausible. H33 is rejected because its entire signed interval fails to support the hypothesized negative association and the point estimate suggests an opposite direction; however, I do not claim a separate opposite association from this one test without follow-up. The only sufficiently promising new secondary signal is H25: outcome_014 feature_065 in feature_043-high samples has a very large signed point estimate (~+0.057, outcome_014 threshold ~0.009), but its interval crosses zero and this arose from multiplicity-heavy screening. I therefore leave H25 active and request independent validation. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset only; feature labels are opaque, subgroup eligibility may select correlated contexts, and I do not interpret these results causally or mechanistically.",
  "research_notes": "Round 3 appraise after new discovery panel: Accepted outcome_013/feature_065 direction -1 associations are now robust across H13 high feature_043, H28 upper-half, H29 unrestricted, and H38 lower-half. H39 median-split interaction is rejected as written; the feature_065/outcome_013 association appears broad rather than stronger specifically in high feature_043. Cross-outcome feature_065 high-feature_043 panel: most outcomes are unresolved deferred because point estimates are small/opposite or intervals are wide and multiple testing is substantial. H33 outcome_011 is rejected because the signed interval does not support the negative-direction hypothesis and suggests an opposite raw pattern, but no reversal is claimed yet. H25 outcome_014 is the only notable new candidate: signed estimate large and well above outcome_014 threshold, but CI crosses zero; validation requested. If H25 validation supports the effect, next consider outcome_014 scope tests (unrestricted, upper-half, lower-half/interaction) before accepting. If H25 validation fails, close outcome_014/feature_065 and keep panel mostly negative. Remaining untested localizations: H37 outcome_013 feature_043<=P75, H43/H44 outcome_006 feature_045 upper/lower feature_043 halves. Current approximate 10% absolute-mean thresholds: outcome_013 ~0.027, outcome_014 ~0.0093, outcome_006 ~0.0093, outcome_011 ~0.030, outcome_008 ~0.028, most other negative-score outcomes ~0.025. Avoid causal/mechanistic interpretation; focus on dataset-internal associations and reproducibility."
